## The implementation

- `apps/storytime/lib/teacher-media.ts` (new). The function `stepMediaOf(step, week)` reads the
  `materials` list of the step, the fixed key at the start of an entry, and the quoted title at
  the end. The key `karaoke videos` opens the song, and the key `book audio` opens a book of the
  week. The first matching entry wins. The rule never reads a step id. The function
  `hasSignedMedia(media, mediaUrls)` reports whether the primary file of a part holds a signed
  URL.
- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/teacher/[level]/[week]/[day]/lesson-flow.tsx`. The flow takes the
  optional prop `mediaUrls`. The step screen root carries `data-step-id` and `data-step-index`. A
  media step shows one control named `Open media`. The control opens the region `The media
  player`, which holds the media title, the control `Close`, and the at-home player of Phase 3
  with the prop `playerMode="class-screen"`. The Escape key closes the player, and the focus
  returns to the control that opened it. The flow stays mounted, so the step, the Thai toggle, and
  the control `Next step` keep their place. A part with no signed URL opens no player, and the
  step shows the English message `This media is not available.` and the Thai message
  `สื่อนี้ยังไม่พร้อม`.
- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/teacher/[level]/[week]/[day]/page.tsx`. The route signs the week
  with `signWeekMedia(loaded.week, {})` and passes `mediaUrls` to the flow. No client code builds
  a URL of the week path.
- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/st/[level]/[week]/song.tsx`,
  `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/st/[level]/[week]/reader.tsx`, and
  `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/st/[level]/[week]/decodable.tsx`. The three players take the
  optional prop `playerMode?: "at-home" | "class-screen"` with the default `"at-home"`. The class
  screen is 1920x1080, so the song uses the regular pair and never the phone pair. The at-home
  markup stays byte for byte the same: the root element carries `data-mode` only in the
  class-screen mode, so the at-home DOM gains no attribute.
- The new controls use the brand classes: amber `#fcd34d` with brown `#92400e` text for the
  `Open media` control, and brown `#92400e` with white text for the `Close` control. No blue
  class.
- No committed Red test changed. No week content, contract, look file, read-along package, or
  `lib/highlight-windows.ts` changed.

