### Player regression, one run

```bash
cd apps/storytime && CI=true ../../node_modules/.bin/vitest run --maxWorkers=1 __tests__/phase3-reader-end.test.tsx __tests__/phase3-song-ui.test.tsx __tests__/phase3-adversarial-r2-song-lines.test.tsx __tests__/phase3-decodable-punct.test.tsx __tests__/phase3-decodable-ui.test.tsx __tests__/phase3-readalong-ui.test.tsx __tests__/phase3-media-src-write.test.tsx __tests__/look-reader-gap.test.tsx __tests__/look-reader-highlight.test.tsx __tests__/look-reader-turn.test.tsx __tests__/look-adversarial-reader.test.tsx __tests__/look-adversarial-song.test.tsx __tests__/look-clip-mode-switch.test.tsx __tests__/look-song-line-offset.test.tsx __tests__/look-song-playing.test.tsx __tests__/look-decodable-case.test.tsx
```

Exit 1. 16 files. 2 failed tests and 74 passed tests. The 2 failures sit in
`phase3-readalong-ui.test.tsx`: `uses slowFile and slowSentences at playback rate one` and
`marks one word in the shipped 0.04-second overlap`. Both read
`SyntaxError: Invalid selector .bg-[#92400e]`.

The failure is pre-existing. With the reader at the role base version, the same file ends with
exit 1, 2 failed tests and 8 passed tests, and the same 2 errors. The cause is the look-track
commit `4da455774`, which changed the current-word class of the read-along package to the
Tailwind value `bg-[#92400e]`. The test builds that class as a CSS selector, and the selector
parser of jsdom rejects it. The orchestrator routes the failure to the look track.

